# <%= current_page.data.title %>

<%= partial('partials/page_toc') %>

Use only the approved DfE account and entitlement. Complete required training and follow DfE data handling
rules before use. Do not use DfE funded access for unrelated personal projects. SSO does not automatically
enforce these usage restrictions.

## Handle data and usage responsibly

- Provide only the information needed. Check that the data classification, model, service and retention
  arrangements are approved before submitting sensitive information. Never include credentials. No training on
  business data does not mean no retention.

- Check the usage or cost information available in your client and account. Follow the communicated allowance
  and request approval before increasing spend. Follow the allowance communicated by your organisation.

- Break work into clear tasks, provide relevant context and review results before repeating requests. If usage
  is unexpectedly high, seek support or training. High usage alone does not prove misuse.

## Review generated changes

Review and test every generated change before accepting or merging it. Copilot
can produce incorrect or insecure code. Content exclusions and instructions are
not substitutes for access controls or approved handling of sensitive information.
Keep CI checks and human review in place.

For access, sign in and a first test prompt, follow
[Getting started with GitHub Copilot](/guides/github/copilot-getting-started/).
For reviews and scanning, follow
[Work safely in DfE repositories](/guides/github/working-safely/).
